      "source": [
        "# Tropical Cyclone Track and Intensity Forecasting with Deep Learning (v2)\n",
        "**Task:** from a cyclone's last 48 h (8 six-hourly observations) forecast **position, wind speed and distance to land at +6/+12/+18/+24 h**, plus the probability of **rapid intensification** and **landfall approach**.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Inputs**\n",
        "- *Storm history* (IBTrACS, NOAA): position, wind, pressure, motion, distance to land (geography), season.\n",
        "- *Environment* (NOAA PSL reanalysis): **sea-surface temperature** (ERSSTv5), **vertical wind shear** (200 minus 850 hPa) and **steering flow** (mean 850/500/200 hPa wind) from NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1, averaged over a 5 degree box around the storm.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Method:** persistence baseline + Ridge + MLP/LSTM/GRU that learn a *correction to persistence*; best architecture trained as a **5-member ensemble** (better accuracy + honest uncertainty); feature-group ablation and permutation importance; calibrated uncertainty circles; event metrics for rapid intensification and landfall.\n",
        "\n",
        "`Runtime > Change runtime type > T4 GPU`, then `Run all`. Allow **40-90 minutes** the first time (most of it downloading reanalysis fields; results are cached in `/content/env_cache.csv`). If the environment download fails, the notebook automatically continues without those fields and says so."
      ]
    },
